WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.121
A large part of recent AI progress comes from deep
learning paired with big data,

00:00:05.201 --> 00:00:08.138
trained by supervised or reinforcement signals.

00:00:08.218 --> 00:00:13.339
These systems are powerful, but they behave very
differently from living systems,

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:18.604
which learn, make associations, and adapt using
sparse data, efficient energy use,

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:20.402
and few training iterations.

00:00:20.482 --> 00:00:24.126
They also forget previous tasks when trained sequentially,

00:00:24.206 --> 00:00:26.887
a problem known as catastrophic forgetting.

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:31.509
Hopfield networks, with unsupervised learning and
an associative memory,

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:34.591
offer a more biologically plausible alternative,

00:00:34.671 --> 00:00:36.967
but their simplest forms are limited,

00:00:37.047 --> 00:00:41.911
storing only about zero point one four times the
number of nodes in patterns,

00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:46.020
and rarely exploit the biological mechanisms that
inspired them.
